To generate an automatic table of contents (TOC) in a LaTeX document, you can use the following commands:

1. In the preamble of your LaTeX document, add the following lines:

```latex
\documentclass{article} % or any other document class you are using

\usepackage{tocloft} % package to customize the table of contents

\begin{document}
```

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command where you want the TOC to appear in your document, usually at the beginning:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tocloft}

\begin{document}
\tableofcontents
```

3. To add a section, use the `\section` command:

```latex
\section{Introduction}
Text for the Introduction section goes here.
```

4. To add a subsection, use the `\subsection` command:

```latex
\section{Section 1}
\subsection{Subsection 1.1}
Text for Subsection 1.1 goes here.

\subsection{Subsection 1.2}
Text for Subsection 1.2 goes here.
```

5. If you want to customize the formatting of the TOC, you can use the following commands:

```latex
\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\normalfont} % change font for section entries
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecfont}{\normalfont} % change font for subsection entries
\renewcommand{\cftsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsecnumwidth}} % add dots for section entries
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsubsecnumwidth}} % add dots for subsection entries
\setlength{\cftsecnumwidth}{2em} % set width of section numbers
\setlength{\cftsubsecnumwidth}{2.5em} % set width of subsection numbers
```

With these commands, your TOC will be automatically generated based on the sections and subsections you add to your document. The final TOC will look like this:

```latex
